            ("Why is whistling strictly forbidden backstage in historic theaters?", "Historically, stagehand flymen were off-duty sailors who communicated scenery drops with whistle codes, so whistling could drop sandbags on actors", ["It irritates the director", "It damages delicate acoustic microphones", "It signals that the show is canceled"], "Sailor flymen moved heavy overhead battens and counterweights upon hearing whistles; an errant whistle could cause fatal scenery drops."),
